<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89852" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσορος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσουρος</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
		</span></i> (v. infr.), once in <i><span class="en">S.,
			<u>Ph.</u>691</span></i>:—
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>adjoining, bordering
			on</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἰγύπτου τὰ πρόσουρα Λιβύῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.18
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				3.97
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				102
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ Ἀραβίῃ, π.
			ἐούσῃ</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ
			Αἰγύπτῳ</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.12
			</span></i>; <i><span class="en">
				X.
			</span></i> in 
				Att.
			 form, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ πρόσορα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					6.1.17
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				36.53
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.177
			</span></i>, etc.:—in <i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i> l.c., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵν᾽ αὐτὸς ἦν πρόσουρος
				οὐκ ἔχων βάσιν, πρόσουρον</span> shd. be read.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
